        "text": " This distorts the intended meaning.\n\n### Why D is Correct:\n**D** correctly uses the **plural subject** *\"female cowbirds\"* to match the plural pronoun *\"their\"* in the non-underlined modifier, and properly conveys that cowbirds lay their eggs **in** the nests of other birds (warblers, vireos, flycatchers, thrushes) \u2014 not that they lay the eggs of those birds.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Key Grammar Concepts Tested:\n1. **Modifier placement** \u2013 An introductory participial phrase must immediately precede the noun it modifies.\n2. **Pronoun-antecedent agreement** \u2013 *Their* (plural) must refer to a plural noun.\n3. **Clarity of reference** \u2013 Avoid ambiguous pronouns like *those* that could point to the wrong noun.\n\nWould you like more practice with similar GMAT Sentence Correction questions?",
