  "answer_text": "It looks like you're referring to a **GMAT Sentence Correction** question! Here is a full breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcdd GMAT Sentence Correction Question\n\n**Full Sentence:**\n\"Unable to build nests or care for their young, a female cowbird lays up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including warblers, vireos, flycatchers, and thrushes.\"\n\n---\n\n## Answer Choices:\n\n\n- **A.** a female cowbird lays up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including\n- **B.** a female cowbird will use the nests of other birds to lay up to 40 eggs a year, including those of\n- **C.** female cowbirds use the nests of other birds to lay up to 40 eggs a year, including those of\n- **D.** female cowbirds lay up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including\n- **E.** up to 40 eggs a year are laid by female cowbirds in the nests of other birds, including\n\n\n\u2705 **Correct Answer: D**\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd0d Explanation:\n\n### Problem 1: Subject-Verb Agreement / Pronoun Agreement\nIn **A** and **B**, *their* (plural) does not agree with *a female cowbird* (singular). So **A and B are eliminated**.\n\n### Problem 2: Dangling/Misplaced Modifier\nThe first major problem is the modifier \"Unable to build nests or care for their young.\" This modifier must be followed by *female cowbirds*. Notice that the modifier says \"care for **their** young,\" so it needs the **plural form** of cowbird.\n\n### Problem 3: Ambiguous Reference in C\nIn **C**, *\"female cowbirds...lay up to 40 eggs a year, including those of warblers\"* \u2014 here, *those* seems to refer to **eggs** (the nearest preceding plural noun), yielding the misleading meaning that female cowbirds lay **the eggs of warblers**. This distorts the intended meaning.\n\n### Why D is Correct:\n**D** correctly uses the **plural subject** *\"female cowbirds\"* to match the plural pronoun *\"their\"* in the non-underlined modifier, and properly conveys that cowbirds lay their eggs **in** the nests of other birds (warblers, vireos, flycatchers, thrushes) \u2014 not that they lay the eggs of those birds.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Key Grammar Concepts Tested:\n1. **Modifier placement** \u2013 An introductory participial phrase must immediately precede the noun it modifies.\n2. **Pronoun-antecedent agreement** \u2013 *Their* (plural) must refer to a plural noun.\n3. **Clarity of reference** \u2013 Avoid ambiguous pronouns like *those* that could point to the wrong noun.\n\nWould you like more practice with similar GMAT Sentence Correction questions?",
